description:
It seems that on the common path, we'll be calling `pak` twice, once without rmarkdown, and again, with rmarkdown. I expect most people will not explicitly add `rmarkdown` to the list, so we should aim to have a single `pak` call for that case. 

E.g.,

1. first call `
```r
res <- tryCatch({
  pak(c(if(!any(grepl("rmarkdown", user_deps)), "rmarkdown", user_deps)
}, 
  error = function(e) {
    pak(c(user_deps))
})
if (!"rmarkdown" %in% res$packages)
  stop("rmarkdown..."
```

but more robust, and better error messages (i.e., surfacing the pak error message correctly for errors)

_Originally posted by @t-kalinowski in https://github.com/t-kalinowski/ir/pull/45#discussion_r3358234054_
